{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, בְּשַׂר","hw":"בְּשַׂר","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בְּשַׂר</span></big>  <strong>n.m. flesh (</strong>𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּסַר</span>, Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܣܰܪ</span>; BH <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּשָׂר</span> √ <span dir=\"rtl\">בשׂר</span><strong>)</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:5\" href=\"/Daniel.7.5\">Dn 7:5</a> <em>flesh</em> (as devoured by beast); emph. <span dir=\"rtl\">בִּשְׂרָא</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:11\" href=\"/Daniel.2.11\">2:11</a> <em>flesh</em> = mankind, <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּל־ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:9\" href=\"/Daniel.4.9\">4:9</a> = all creatures.","next":"BDB Aramaic, בַּת","prev":"BDB Aramaic, בַּר³"}